# Edge-case oracle-fodder for tools/check_natural_save.sh (bd inc-e68f).
#
# Tanglefoot (tools/keys/natural-save-tangle.keys) proves the invariant holds
# on ordinary DC 15 saves, but a modest DC and a modest save bonus can never
# by itself DISTINGUISH the fix from the defect: Bonus + 20 clears DC 15
# either way, so a natural 20 there "succeeds" whether or not the special
# case exists. Proving the check can actually go red needs a DC far enough
# above the subject's bonus that a bare Bonus + 20 comparison would read
# FAILURE on a natural 20 -- exactly the case the SRD forbids.
#
# "guardian runes" (lib/dungeon.irh) rolls Fortitude or Will, DC 27, on
# every move within it, chosen at random per step -- comfortably out of
# reach of a level 1 paladin's +3 base. Pinned to seed 4 because the result
# is otherwise a coin flip: this exact seed, key sequence and settings
# combination is known (and re-verified when this file was written) to roll
# a natural 20 within six exposures, printing "Will Save: 1d20 (20) +3
# base = 23 vs DC 27 [failure]." on the unfixed engine and "...[success]."
# on the fixed one -- the smoking gun tools/check_natural_save.sh
# --prove-red reads. Six exposures cost the subject about half his hit
# points (31 -> 15 measured); this file does not run more than that.
#
# Freeze Monsters is on so nothing else moves while this runs.

@include chargen-paladin.keys
@until "Afoot" ESC

w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10
SPACE
ESC

w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT
ENTER
L
w
@choose "Change terrain type"
RIGHT RIGHT
ENTER
L
@dump:terrain-made

RIGHT
@while "Confirm" y
@dump:entry

RIGHT
LEFT
RIGHT
LEFT
RIGHT
LEFT

v
@dump:messages
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
